# Build context is the repository root; keep everything generated, local or
# secret out of the image.
**/node_modules
**/.git
**/.next
**/build
**/coverage
**/dist
**/out
**/data
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.test.example
**/.claude
**/CLAUDE.md
**/AGENTS.md
*.pre-monorepo

# The runtime stage copies whole workspaces, so anything not excluded here ships
# to production. Prose first:
**/reports
**/docs
**/TODO.md
**/i18n-db.txt

# Then the test suite — the largest thing in the back-end and served by nothing.
#
# `tsconfig.json` includes `**/*.ts`, so the `verify` stage's `tsc --noEmit` did
# incidentally type-check these; that is not what that stage is FOR (it is the
# route-table/schema consistency check named in the Dockerfile), and CI's
# `bun run lint` type-checks the suite on every push regardless.
#
# `check-coverage.ts` has to go with it: it is the one non-test file that
# imports a test helper (`../tests/helpers/coverage`), so excluding `tests/`
# alone makes `bun run build` fail on a missing module. Verified by reproducing
# the verify stage locally with both moved aside — `bun run build` exits 0.
**/tests
apps/back-end/scripts/check-coverage.ts
